a52sxq: glink_pkt: no second unlock on the O_NONBLOCK empty-queue path

glink_pkt_read() drops gpdev->lock before it looks at the queue; the O_NONBLOCK path for an
empty queue unlocked it again. Unlocking a mutex that another task (write, poll, ioctl, the
rpdev remove during SSR) holds breaks its mutual exclusion (audit 2026-11-18, low 24).

--- a/drivers/rpmsg/glink_pkt.c
+++ b/drivers/rpmsg/glink_pkt.c
@@ -496,7 +496,7 @@
 	if (skb_queue_empty(&gpdev->queue) && !gpdev->rskb) {
 		if (file->f_flags & O_NONBLOCK) {
 			spin_unlock_irq(&gpdev->queue_lock);
-			mutex_unlock(&gpdev->lock);
+			/* a52sxq: gpdev->lock was already dropped above; no second unlock */
 			return -EAGAIN;
 		}
 
